umul-s: x * y, for x and y from 0 to 999 with x * y <= 999; x may also be negative.
Cells 82-98. To call it, put y in cell 96, load x into the accumulator and JMP 82.
It returns x * y in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99, including y in cell 96 (counted down to 0).
Size 17 cells. It runs at most 8,002 instructions, 1,011.4 on average, counted from cell 82 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 82     695      STO 95   cells 82-84: the call: store x, and copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98
 83     199      CLA 99
 84     698      STO 98
 85     404      SFT 04   cells 85-93: p = 0 by SFT 04; then add x to p and take 1 from y until y is used up
 86     694      STO 94
 87     196      CLA 96
 88     700      SUB 00
 89     397      TAC 97
 90     696      STO 96
 91     194      CLA 94
 92     295      ADD 95
 93     886      JMP 86
 94     000      data: the product p
 95     000      data: x
 96     000      data: y, counted down to 0
 97     194      CLA 94   cell 97: the product into the accumulator
 98     000               set on every call: the jump back to the caller
